WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:24.870
<i>At this moment, our efforts are finally being rewarded.</i>

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.830
<i>The long and hard battles,
the treachery...</i>

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:31.070
<i>...and even the number of deaths.
Everything was forgotten.</i>

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:34.970
<i>We stood there captivated
before the shining treasure.</i>

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.910
Treasure
Island

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.710
Takarajima

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.520
saa ikou

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.520
Come, let's go

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:52.610
yume ni mita shima heto

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:52.610
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.450
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.450
Across the waves, on the wind

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.330
umi hedeyou

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.330
We'll travel the oceans

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.250
ikute ni wa

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.250
Many of us

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.250
minna mada shiranai

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.250
Still don't know of

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:09.000
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:09.000
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.500
matte iru darou

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.500
That await us there

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:15.010
itsumo shinji you

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:15.010
We must always have trust

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.260
magokoro wo

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.260
And be sincere

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:24.520
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:24.520
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.650
tade hitotsu no

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.650
I only...

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.070
akogare dake wa

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.070
...have one desire

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.360
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.360
And no one...

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:40.070
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:40.070
...will ever take it away

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.620
tade hitotsu no

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.620
I only...

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.920
akogare dake wa

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.920
...have one desire

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.250
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.250
And no one...

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:59.180
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:59.180
...will ever take it away

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:10.480
episode

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:10.480
Until We Meet Again,
\h             Sea Breeze

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:25.370
The Hispaniola is leaving!

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.780
The ship leaves and the gulls remain.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.100
The gulls who have lost their wings.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.800
I-It's impossible!

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:42.010
Ahoy!

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:44.520
We're still alive!

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.350
Don't leave us here!

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.190
Bring us back to England!

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.000
Ahoy!

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.600
Ahoy!

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.430
Ahoy!

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.190
It's no use!
They can't see us anymore.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:01.700
Fifteen men...

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.880
...on a dead man's chest.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.800
I don't want to die abandoned on this island!

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.680
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.210
I want to go back home,
even if I have to be hanged!

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.850
<i>We've loaded the treasure onto the Hispaniola...</i>

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.050
<i>...and set our course for England.</i>

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:32.690
<i>Fear, sadness and moments of joy.</i>

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.930
<i>We'd known it all, but now it was time...</i>

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.650
<i>...to leave Treasure Island.</i>

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:40.820
Goodbye, Treasure Island!

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:43.810
<i>Farewell...</i>

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:46.290
<i>What an adventure it was,
my dear island.</i>

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.860
<i>Furthermore, our story
was far from being over,</i>

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:52.610
<i>because we couldn't agree on what to do with Silver.</i>

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:56.330
<i>Many wanted to leave him on the island since taking him to trial was dangerous.</i>

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.810
<i>But on the other hand,
he did help us find the treasure,</i>

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:02.760
<i>so we tied him up and took him on board.</i>

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:08.300
<i>Unable to decide his fate, we put him in the hold for the time being.</i>

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.060
Pieces of eight!

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.540
Pieces of eight!

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:17.780
<i>As for our other problem child...</i>

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:21.690
<i>"Seagull" Puppy hadn't lost his spirit...</i>

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.570
<i>...and seemed determined to get back on the right path.</i>

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.690
<i>He wouldn't get his share of the treasure,</i>

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:29.910
<i>but he wouldn't be turned over to the police.</i>

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:41.250
<i>Ben Gunn was the new subject of conversation.</i>

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.330
<i>With clothes from Mr. Trelawney,</i>

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.640
<i>he strutted about for the first time in 10 years.</i>

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:58.060
<i>We all thought that the return to Bristol would be smooth sailing from here on out.</i>

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.530
<i>But Silver alone had other plans.</i>

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.490
Hey, Gray!

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.580
Take me for a walk on the deck.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.540
I want to see the sun set.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:15.650
I beg you. Either way,
when we reach England,

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:17.560
I'll be hanged or imprisoned for life at best.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:20.740
I just want to say goodbye to
the Southern sea's sunset.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.220
It really is nice to breathe the air on deck.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.230
Hey, Jim...

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.150
And? Did you get
the share you deserved?

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.390
Your young age mustn't
prevent you from claiming it.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:46.010
You too did your part of the work.

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:49.720
We're going to give all of
the treasure to the Crown.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.160
Really, to the Crown?

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:58.000
Then she can decide who gets it on our return.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.600
That way we can avoid any dispute.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:02.380
That was Dr. Livesey's idea.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.230
I can't believe it.
What a waste...

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:08.130
If you do that, you'll hardly get anything.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:13.540
But hey, that's your business.
Doesn't matter to me at all.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.290
Many men have lost their lives...

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:40.840
Someone once said:

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:43.440
"If this world were made of gold,

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:48.380
men would be ready to die for a handful of mud."

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:55.310
From where we stand, we can't see the island anymore.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.200
I've failed.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:00.940
This time, even the famous one-legged man has lost.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.500
Come on, Gray.
Cut it out already.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.280
We're in the middle of the ocean.
Where do you expect me to go?

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:24.590
It's all over for me.
You know that, right?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:29.120
What I know, is that John Silver...

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:32.280
...has gotten out of worse situations than this.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:33.510
So I'm remaining cautious.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.100
I'd very much like to resemble this
John Silver that you say you know.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.650
Hey, wait, Gray!

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:50.610
Mr. Trelawney and Dr. Livesey haven't forgotten their promise, I hope?

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.610
You know, I solved the map's riddle.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:56.910
So they promised to defend me at trial.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:00.830
I have no desire to die at the end of a rope!

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:12.790
Well... of course no one wants to die at the end of a rope.

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:16.050
But...
But, I-I...

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:20.430
I really hate to see Silver reduced to this!

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.350
I hate to see it, too.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:23.930
What has become of Silver.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:27.400
No, I would even say it's disgraceful of him.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:35.770
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:40.290
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:53.670
Come, follow me.

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:54.680
Where to?

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.600
To look for the old Silver.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.730
What is it?
Mr. Trelawney want to talk to me?

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:05.390
He's waiting for you on deck.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:08.900
Okay, I'll be there in a second.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:18.280
Wh-Where is Mr. Trelawney?

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:21.450
It's time, Jim.
Watch.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:22.200
Okay.

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:32.930
Hey, what's the matter with you, Gray?

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.290
Fight back, Silver!

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.600
We'll fight!
One on one!

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.980
That's enough.
I'm not in the mood to fight.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:53.570
Right now, my mind's on my trial.

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:55.030
That's a lie!

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:57.150
No matter how well you pretend to be the beaten dog,

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:58.530
you're not fooling me!

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:07.670
Ouch, that hurt!

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:10.250
Hey, I really felt that one.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:14.210
You might want to stop or you'll break my nice nose.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:15.880
Stand up, Silver!
Stand up!

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:20.090
Alright, I understand, Gray.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.170
If I continue to let you do this,

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:24.200
I'm gonna end up in pieces.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:28.850
Whipped dog or not, I still have to defend myself.

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:34.170
You see, Jim.
He hasn't changed at all.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:35.930
He's far from giving up.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:40.140
In order to let us drop our guard,
he played the part of whipped dog!

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.800
Your fists can't lie!

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.890
Your tricks won't work on us, Silver!

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:49.350
You flatter me, Gray.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.560
But I believe that you've overestimated me.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.660
I never tire of seeing this beauty!

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:15.880
Still admiring diamonds?

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.210
Well, you know...

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.960
We've decided to give it all to the Crown.

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:22.720
Stop admiring it.
You'll get too attached.

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:27.360
We'll stop at the West Indies come nightfall.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:30.270
Once there, we'll have a
serious problem to tackle.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.810
A serious problem?

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:32.520
Yes...

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:36.230
In addition to supplies,
we need to recruit sailors.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:40.190
And for that, we need an experienced old sea dog.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:44.150
Unfortunately, only one man aboard
the Hispaniola fits this description.

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:45.660
Silver?

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:46.680
Exactly.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:50.120
You're going to let that
dangerous villain disembark?

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:54.010
Dr. Livesey himself admits we have no choice.

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:58.880
Now this is good stuff.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:02.240
The perfect blend of mocha.

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:04.720
Who made it?
Was it you, Jim?

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:05.400
Yeah.

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:07.790
I see.
Much appreciated.

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:12.890
I would like it very much if you could answer a question:

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:18.360
According to you, Silver, what is
the thing that matters the most?

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:28.800
Right now, this cup of coffee.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:30.280
Answer seriously!

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:32.320
I am serious, Jim.

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:34.910
For what it's worth, the thing I wanted most when I spoke,

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:38.150
was this cup of coffee that you made.

00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:44.560
But tomorrow, that'll surely change.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:49.000
In other words, I don't really know...

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:51.800
...what matters the most to me.

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:55.840
That's why I continue to look for it, day after day.

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:59.730
Finding Flint's treasure was my obsession for ten years.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:06.800
By finding it, I had hoped to discover what matters the most to me.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:08.700
But I haven't found it.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.720
And even if I had gotten my hands on Flint's treasure,

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:15.660
none of its jewels could have made me wealthy.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.620
This isn't what I was searching for.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.800
But it exists, Jim.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:34.550
I don't know where, but one day, I hope to discover what matters the most to me.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:38.560
If I don't...

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:45.400
If I don't,

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:48.490
it'll be too sad.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:58.380
That's the situation, Silver.
We'd like to give you this job.

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:02.790
Understood. I need to recruit sailors and buy supplies.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.590
But if you ever...

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:07.840
Rest assured, owner Trelawney.
I won't run away.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:10.640
In fact, I'm glad to be able to help you.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:16.720
That way, you'll defend me more eagerly at my trial back home.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.190
Please take this is consideration.

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:25.050
Bear in mind, we're taking precautions during your time on land.

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:29.990
I see.
This is one beautiful accessory.

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.290
You can spend the night in the port.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:36.910
You have until 10 am tomorrow morning to fix everything and get back on board.

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:45.340
Who wants my bananas?

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:48.800
Real silk!
Top quality from Asia!

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.220
Anyone want to buy a pearl necklace?

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:59.810
All your ladies love to wear necklaces.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:09.080
Anyone want to buy a pearl necklace?

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:25.130
<i>This city holds the port where we made our last stop on the way to the island.</i>

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:29.400
<i>I was kidnapped and it was Silver who came to save me.</i>

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.710
<i>In this city full of memories.</i>

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:35.010
We'll recruit sailors first.

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:38.210
We can buy supplies tomorrow.

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:40.870
You can find the best products at the morning market.

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:45.730
<i>Silver went around to the taverns to recruit sailors.</i>

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:48.690
She's called the Hispaniola.
Where are you from?

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:52.150
The pay is what you'd expect,
but the pittance is good.

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:54.610
<i>We went from tavern to tavern.</i>

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:59.740
The departure is at 10 am.
The captain is called Smollett.

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:01.710
He has a nasty mood,

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:04.090
but you can count on him
in stormy weather.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:07.670
<i>It's the necklace vendor from the port.</i>

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:11.040
<i>She's beautiful...</i>

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:15.080
That's it.
Any questions?

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:20.890
<i>After that, we visited a lot of taverns....</i>

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:23.980
<i>...and when we arrived at our inn,
it was already dark.</i>

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:32.900
<i>Even Silver was tired from walking and dragging that ball and chain.</i>

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:41.210
In total, we found nine good sailors.

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:43.850
They'll meet us at the port at 9 am.

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:45.900
Gray, Jim, you better remember that.

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:48.500
My memory falters sometimes.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:53.920
Before that, we'll go to the market and look at meat and fruit.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.720
And with that, my work will be finished.

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:00.770
Bottom's up, Gray.

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:03.690
I stole this bottle from the last tavern.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:07.640
Whad'ya say? A little celebration for the formation of the new crew.

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:10.860
Very well.

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:31.200
I couldn't, it's the kid's turn.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:32.100
I see.

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:33.400
R-Really, me too...?

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:36.050
Rum might be a little too strong for children, though.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.240
Thank you very much!

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:42.930
<i>So good.</i>

00:18:58.150 --> 00:19:01.110
Dont worry, there's more where that came from.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.920
Finally, one down.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:19.100
Alright! Just us two now, Gray.
Let's drink the rest.

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:20.630
Very well, my thoughts exactly.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:31.000
I commend you, Gray.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:34.360
Few men can compete with me when it comes to the bottle.

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:39.110
When I drink, you drink.
And when you drink, I drink.

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:41.360
We'll see who collapses first.

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:44.560
It's a duel.
I know what you're doing, Silver.

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:46.660
You're trying to get me drunk.

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:49.630
Then you'll be able to escape, right?

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:53.630
You got me, Gray.
Good job seeing through me.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:55.830
But you won't be able to.

00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:57.630
You'll collapse first.

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:06.680
That vendor with the shawl.
She's your wife, isn't she?

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:10.550
I've heard the rumour, you know.

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:14.900
It's said that a "one-legged man" is married to a beautiful métisse.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:20.830
Go ahead, Gray.
I've had my drink, it's your turn.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:22.000
Alright.

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:25.240
You see that, Silver?

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.190
I saw it.

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:28.750
Good.
Then, now it's your—

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:36.750
Sweet dreams, Gray.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.870
You didn't have to come all this way.

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:04.990
You could have waited for me at the Spyglass.

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:09.650
Ships heading south are always stopping here.

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:12.450
All the sailors' wives know that.

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:16.310
Still, even if you know we're waiting for you,

00:21:16.310 --> 00:21:18.420
you're not the type to come back.

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:21.070
You know me so well.

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:23.380
You're not my wife for nothing.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:41.860
Silver!

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:43.820
Silver!

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:48.780
Hey, head for the hull of Hispaniola.

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:51.790
My share of the treasure is still on board.

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:54.020
Silver!

00:21:54.470 --> 00:21:56.210
Silver!

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:59.960
SILVER!

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:10.640
I-It's gone!

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:12.510
There was a chest right here!

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:14.850
Look, it's vanished!

00:22:15.630 --> 00:22:17.300
<i>Silver had disappeared.</i>

00:22:17.300 --> 00:22:20.940
<i>He parted from our company along with his share of the treasure.</i>

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:24.400
My friend... Silver!

00:22:28.520 --> 00:22:32.370
To      be        continued

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:38.400
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:38.400
Hey sea breeze

00:22:38.400 --> 00:22:44.210
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:38.400 --> 00:22:44.210
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:45.430 --> 00:22:50.420
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:45.430 --> 00:22:50.420
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:55.860
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:55.860
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.860 --> 00:23:01.270
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.860 --> 00:23:01.270
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:06.730
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:06.730
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.730 --> 00:23:12.360
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.730 --> 00:23:12.360
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.360 --> 00:23:18.220
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:12.360 --> 00:23:18.220
Will be brought back

00:23:19.310 --> 00:23:24.810
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:19.310 --> 00:23:24.810
The sunset on my back

00:23:24.810 --> 00:23:30.700
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:24.810 --> 00:23:30.700
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:40.420
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:40.420
I blow out a whistle

00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:48.440
He disappeared without even saying goodbye.

00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:49.900
Ten years have passed.

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:52.480
Treasure Island is nothing but a distant memory.

00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:54.740
During that time, I became a sailor...

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:58.200
...and while in a port,
I hear an unforgettable voice.

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:00.890
Is it a dream or an illusion?

00:24:01.640 --> 00:24:05.170
The final episode of Treasure Island:
"Flint Can't Fly Anymore"

00:24:05.930 --> 00:24:09.760
Nothing or no one, can ever take away the taste of adventure!

00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:13.760
m 0 0 l 960 0 960 720 0 720

00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:13.760
*

00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:13.760
Next time

00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:13.760
Coming soon!

00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:13.760
Flint
Can't Fly Anymore
